  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">An uptick in maritime incidents around Hormuz drives higher insurance and security burdens and diverts salvage and crew resources to the Gulf, which in turn reduces vessel calls, crew availability and service capacity at transshipment and regional ports serving the Russia–Ukraine theatre, lowering their operational capacity.</data>
