  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A rise in cross‑border military incidents normalizes coercive use of force and reinforces incentives for actors to employ or threaten maritime interdiction as leverage, raising the intensity and political willingness to impose blockade-like pressure in Hormuz.</data>
